      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-04-30T01:50:28.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"defeateddust\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/defeateddust/48/2245_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> defeateddust:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fun thing if you have savage mana before the dreamer flips with ten projections under it and it doesnt get destroyed you can use savage mana on another projection or enviroment target and immediatly win</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>H=5.&nbsp; Fanatic, Scholar, and Omnitron-X with two other heroes.&nbsp; Fanatic must be at least third in the turn rotation.&nbsp; Fanatic plays End of Days on turn one.&nbsp; The Dreamer flips, and plays 3 Violent Nightmares and another Projection.&nbsp; Scholar plays Don't Dismiss Anything to put Fanatic's End of Days back on top of her deck, Omnitron-X Timeshifts it into play.&nbsp; Do anything but destroy The Dreamer/Fanatic/End of Days, and don't remove any Projections from the board via non-destruction effects.&nbsp; By the start of the environment you have won the game in two rounds.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
